==Enemy==
M. Ost has high health, moderate damage, extremely fast movement speed and attacks, decent range and guaranteed knockback + slow + curse, all of which allows him to wreak havoc upon your units if not dealt with properly. His biggest weakness is that he has a whopping 10 knockbacks despite his health, making him manageable if you lock him in a knockback cycle with many attackers. Ironically, this weakness may even become a strength, as his high knockback count can put your attackers at risk of pushing into the range of an enemy backliner.

==Strategy==
Although M. Ost appears on paper to be R.Ost on steroids, he really isn't as terrifying as he may seem, as there are actually more [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relics]] than [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless units]]. His guaranteed knockback and slow can help push your more expensive ranged attackers back into safety when they're hit, making [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] a good counter to him. Once you have a sizeable stack of mid-ranged attackers, you should be able to knock him back before he destroys your cats. His slow ability also somewhat alleviates the suicidal tendency of fast ranged attackers, such as [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]], [[Kachi-Kachi (Uber Rare Cat)|Fire Squad Kachiyama]] and [[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber CC]], as they won't rush back into his attacks until the effect ends.

If the stage gives you the option to stack [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]], that can also be used to keep M. Ost constantly knocked back or crowd-controlled. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] in particular works very well against him. If you've finished the daunting process of clearing all 4-Crown [[Stories of Legend]] stages, including the [[Eldritch Forces/Invasion|Eldritch Forces Invasion]], [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] is a fantastic counter to M. Ost, due to her massive damage and short attack animation. However, timing is an absolute must for rushers, including Idi:N2, as M. Ost outranges them, unless you have some [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|freeze]] [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|effects]] at hand to paralyze M. Ost.

